id: pm-2sef82
title: "GH-1356: SDK: expose the canonical settings preview through host-bound audited mutation"
description: Expose an opt-in canonical settings preview through the injected audited extension command SDK.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,context-management,github-intake
created_at: "2026-09-30T06:48:43.202Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-03T20:57:03.173Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#c34534ca90095a05f3a48f57"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "An opt-in host-bound preview matches actual canonical persistence for named and custom presets; Ordinary mutation receipts remain bounded and backwards compatible; Preview is read-only for settings and immutable history; Invalid settings, locks, concurrency and replay retain existing guarantees; A copied packed extension without a local SDK import demonstrates preview parity"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: A copied extension can obtain the exact validated effective settings preview through the host capability without duplicate normalization or a local SDK runtime import.
actual_result: "Reporter independently observed a dry-run boolean receipt without canonical settings on published 2026.9.30. Named governance preset normalization is correct, but the callback proposal differs from the effective persisted result. No settings/history preview writes were reported. Current-tree design and implementation are pending."
